WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
Your AI says the code is ready.

2
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.600
Every test passes.

3
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:04.800
Would you merge it?

4
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.360
CrossExam puts the tests on trial.

5
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.160
This cache change passes all four tests.

6
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:15.120
But two customers reuse a request ID, and one gets the other's reservation.

7
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.080
CrossExam proves it with just two requests.

8
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.240
Then it strengthens the tests.

9
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.320
New versions must catch more bugs while correct code keeps passing.

10
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.600
This weaker version?

11
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:26.800
Rejected.

12
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.280
Finally, a separate audit: 1 out of 8 bugs caught becomes 7.

13
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.360
No correct controls rejected.

14
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.880
It's a small synthetic benchmark, and we show the miss, too.

15
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.520
Subquadratic helps decide where to look.

16
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.640
This run uses seeded bugs and test proposals.

17
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.520
OpenUI lets you inspect every result.

18
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:46.720
CrossExam.

19
00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.320
Don't just trust the score.

20
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.840
Make it prove something.
